  ],
  "description": "One channel of the Sontec 432C/9 family. The Sontec MES-430C audio board SPN 1110-0945-00 Rev A supplies the differential receiver, shelving amplifier, three adjustable bridged feedback resonators, shared summing stage and servo timing. The related MEP-250A wiring documents the off-board frequency and width controls. Frequency and gain decks use continuous tracking controls in place of the factory switched resistors. The bass shelf has 50 and 100 Hz settings and the treble shelf uses a fixed nominal 10 kHz corner. The shelf RC values and front-panel resistor assumptions set those corners. NE5532 and TL07x/TL06x cards proxy the sealed HS2030, HS6000 and original servo devices. Vactrol switching and servo trim injection use electrical equivalents. Mono line I/O and ideal supply rails.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Low Shelf Gain",
      "High Shelf Gain",
      "Low Bell Gain",
      "Low Bell Frequency",
      "Low Bell Bandwidth",
      "Mid Bell Gain",
      "Mid Bell Frequency",
      "Mid Bell Bandwidth",
      "High Bell Gain",
      "High Bell Frequency",
      "High Bell Bandwidth"
    ],
    "switches": [
      "Low Shelf 100 Hz",
      "Bell Bands Bypass",
      "Shelf Bands Bypass",
      "EQ Bypass"
    ]
  },
